//Multi-declarator locals must decompose into AssignStmts that execute
//in DECLARATOR order: each initializer sees the earlier declarators'
//already-assigned values (b = a * 3 with a = 2 is 6, c = b + 4 is 10).
//Regression: the decomposition used to re-derive the insertion point
//per declarator, placing each later assign BEFORE the earlier ones.
import io;
int main() {
    int a = 2, b = a * 3, c = b + 4;
    io.print(a);
    io.print(b);
    io.print(c);
    return c;
}
